docs/gitlab-release.md-81-
docs/gitlab-release.md-82-1. `validate` runs shell lint, Swift tests, a Swift build, and an ad-hoc-signed
docs/gitlab-release.md-83-   universal development bundle without production credentials.
docs/gitlab-release.md:84:2. `release_v0_2_0` runs only for the protected `v0.2.0` tag on the trusted
docs/gitlab-release.md:85:   `macos` + `relux-release` runner. It compares GitLab's actual host, project
docs/gitlab-release.md-86-   path, checked-out commit, and runner tags with the protected expected
docs/gitlab-release.md-87-   values. It imports the certificate into a disposable keychain; builds both
docs/gitlab-release.md:88:   `arm64` and `x86_64`; signs with the exact Relux Works Developer ID; submits
docs/gitlab-release.md:89:   the DMG with `notarytool`; requires `Accepted`; saves the notarization log;
docs/gitlab-release.md-90-   staples and validates the ticket; runs Gatekeeper; and produces checksums.
docs/gitlab-release.md-91-3. `verify_v0_2_0` first requires the Release metadata to name exactly the
docs/gitlab-release.md-92-   expected same-project Generic Package Registry links, then downloads all
docs/gitlab-release.md-93-   three assets through the job-token-supported Releases API endpoint
docs/gitlab-release.md:94:   `CI_API_V4_URL/projects/$CI_PROJECT_ID/releases/$CI_COMMIT_TAG/downloads/<asset>`.
docs/gitlab-release.md:95:   Browser-style `/-/releases/` permanent links remain end-user URLs and are
docs/gitlab-release.md-96-   not used as authenticated CI API targets. Redirects are followed manually
docs/gitlab-release.md-97-   with a fixed hop limit: `JOB-TOKEN` is attached only when the next request
docs/gitlab-release.md:98:   has the exact confirmed GitLab origin, while an external HTTPS object-storage
docs/gitlab-release.md-99-   URL is fetched without that header. Unsafe, malformed, missing, excessive,
docs/gitlab-release.md-100-   or unexpected redirects fail closed. The job verifies that the Release points
docs/gitlab-release.md:101:   to the accepted commit, compares the published checksum file with the
docs/gitlab-release.md-102-   CI-produced file, checks both hashes, and proves the stable and versioned
docs/gitlab-release.md-103-   DMGs are byte-identical.
docs/gitlab-release.md-104-
docs/gitlab-release.md-105-Production jobs are serialized through the
docs/gitlab-release.md:106:`relux-production-release` resource group. The certificate and API key are
docs/gitlab-release.md-107-decoded only under a `mktemp` directory; the temporary keychain and decoded
docs/gitlab-release.md-108-files are removed by an exit trap.
docs/gitlab-release.md-109-
docs/gitlab-release.md-110-The package upload uses the automatically scoped `CI_JOB_TOKEN`, following the
docs/gitlab-release.md:111:GitLab Generic Package Registry contract:
docs/gitlab-release.md-112-<https://docs.gitlab.com/user/packages/generic_packages/>.
docs/gitlab-release.md-113-Uploads do not follow redirects and require the registry's exact `201` response,
docs/gitlab-release.md-114-so the custom token cannot be forwarded to another origin.
docs/gitlab-release.md:115:The GitLab Release exposes the package objects as direct asset links:
docs/gitlab-release.md:116:<https://docs.gitlab.com/api/releases/links/>.
